 "title": "The composed-epoch native runner executes, and three stage rows it backs still read unassessed",
 "why": "Card CT-COMPOSED-NATIVE (wave 32), its own follow-on. The runner really compiles and runs an admitted case's emitted C under the platform sanitizers and byte-compares stdout with that module's checked task half - and three stage rows it backs still read `unassessed`. A stage may read `executed` only where a named workspace test runs it on the case's own artifact (constraint 23), so the gap is between evidence that exists and evidence that is CREDITED. DISCHARGE: credit the rows in a stage-evidence record, or state why the runner does not back them.",
 "source": "docs/reports/ct-composed-native/README.md",
