{
 "id": "CT-COMPOSED-NATIVE-NON-LINUX-VACUOUS-PASS",
 "title": "The composed-epoch native runner passes green on Windows while asserting nothing",
 "why": "`run_composed_native` in compiler/tests/ct_corpus.rs early-returns on non-Linux/macOS hosts, printing an eprintln, and the test still PASSES. Card STABILITY-REEVAL-1 (wave 34) records this as a disclosure gap rather than a defect: the restriction is documented (evidence_target=linux) and deliberate. But the ledger's CT row publishes 'sanitized-native 9 of 45' with NO platform qualifier, so a green suite on Windows reads as evidence for the CT22/CT25 sanitized rows when it is evidence for nothing. The cadence's rule is that an arm no test reaches is not verified by a green suite; here the suite is green precisely where it reaches nothing. Discharge: state the platform boundary in the CT ledger row beside the sanitized-native count, so the number carries the host condition it was measured on.",
 "source": "docs/reports/stability-reeval-1/README.md",
 "recorded_by": "STABILITY-REEVAL-1"
}
