 "why": "MEASURED by card STABILITY-REEVAL-4 (wave 40). 0d9e922f (CT07) and 45a33285 (CT42) state integration figures - 4620 / 138 at f1fcd14d and 4703 / 140 at ecfef946 - each differing from that card's own gate.json (4644 / 138 and 4697 / 140), and neither publishes a docs/reports/<card>/integration-gate.json. Both cited tips are non-ancestors of main (INTEGRATION-TIP-CITATION-UNREACHABLE), so those two figures have no record outside an unreachable commit's message. AGENTS.md describes the convention as covering 'the three integration gates the integrator measured at the merges where no card's gate could agree with the merged tree', which is true of the three that were published and silent about these two. The CLAUDE.md convention the wave-39 close wrote says an integrator who cannot regenerate the matrix with any card's gate.json measures the tip and writes the file; it does not say what to do when the integrator measures a tip for another reason. DISCHARGE: publish an integration-gate.json for every merge that measures a tip, OR state the rule that a merge whose message states a figure differing from the card's gate must publish one, and apply it retrospectively to these two by a dated appended note (constraint 21).",
 "source": "docs/reports/stability-reeval-4/README.md",
